{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/127255-the-mercenaries","id":127255,"title":"The Mercenaries","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-06T22:18:42-07:00","id":127255,"title":"The Mercenaries","content":"<i>They're scattered everywhere. Some of them wait in a bar in Thailand, drinking their rum as they wait for the next job. Some have a respectable office in Stuttgart, a legitimate security company with special services offered. Others simply wait for the phone to ring, buy their ticket, and ride the ride to the end. They don't need to care about the greater struggle of the Vigil as long as the check clears in time. Their morals are their own, and their targets are usually dead. They are the mercenaries, and they do it their way.</i><br /> <br /> Just an idea I've had kicking around for a while now, how would you envision a mercenary hunter cell/compact. Not just &quot;bounty hunters&quot; like the Knights of St. Adrian, but more like Hellsing's Wild Geese; bog standard mortals who are purely in it for the money, with their morality second?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/483-flyboy254","name":"Flyboy254","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar483_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"703"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T05:53:11-07:00","id":127410,"title":"","content":"So in Dogs of War, there's a clued-in private security firm called &quot;Blackfire&quot;, obviously modeled on Blackwater. It was a little more limited in its initial implementation - the leader was supernatural (some unique deal) and had a specific agenda. I'd just expand it out. It's a private security firm that knows about the supernatural, and caters to very obscure customers who need private supernatural security. Businessman A runs afoul of a vampire plot, and has a business card from an eccentric in Dubai he was told to use if he ever &quot;ran into anything weird&quot; during a night of drunken revelry. He makes the call and signs a check before the Invictus gets to him, and suddenly he has bodyguards packing MP7s, kevlar vests...and incendiary munitions. Elder Vampire B has a longstanding security arrangement with Blackfire. Masquerade violation technically, but they keep the secret and keep him safe, and he's the most powerful local Invictus, so no one bothers him about it. I would say Blackfire makes a good Compact-level group of ex-military/paramilitary types, who had a first encounter, were found by Blackfire instead of Valkyrie (more international in flavor than TFV, as well) and given huge paychecks to do the same job they did before, just weirder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/543-professor-phobos","name":"Professor Phobos","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T09:44:12-07:00","id":127542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/127255-the-mercenaries?p=127410#post127410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in Dogs of War, there's a clued-in private security firm called &quot;Blackfire&quot;, obviously modeled on Blackwater. It was a little more limited in its initial implementation - the leader was supernatural (some unique deal) and had a specific agenda. I'd just expand it out. It's a private security firm that knows about the supernatural, and caters to very obscure customers who need private supernatural security. Businessman A runs afoul of a vampire plot, and has a business card from an eccentric in Dubai he was told to use if he ever &quot;ran into anything weird&quot; during a night of drunken revelry. He makes the call and signs a check before the Invictus gets to him, and suddenly he has bodyguards packing MP7s, kevlar vests...and incendiary munitions. Elder Vampire B has a longstanding security arrangement with Blackfire. Masquerade violation technically, but they keep the secret and keep him safe, and he's the most powerful local Invictus, so no one bothers him about it. I would say Blackfire makes a good Compact-level group of ex-military/paramilitary types, who had a first encounter, were found by Blackfire instead of Valkyrie (more international in flavor than TFV, as well) and given huge paychecks to do the same job they did before, just weirder.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely would agree here. Blackfire has all the trappings of becoming an actual Hunter group, and could easily be catapulted from proto-compact to compact status.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T20:08:40-07:00","id":127944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Professor Phobos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/127255-the-mercenaries?p=127410#post127410\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So in Dogs of War, there's a clued-in private security firm called &quot;Blackfire&quot;, obviously modeled on Blackwater.</div> </div> </div> </div>At my own table, I've reimagined Blackfire as the private-sector arm of VALKYRIE - they're one of the Contractors that form the steering committee and actually oversee and fund VALKYRIE from within the Military Industrial Complex (Vampires are not in-charge of VALKYRIE, but several of these contractors are complicit with vampiric financial interests, and do &quot;keep the peace&quot; by steering VALKYRIE in directions away from those interests and toward their enemies).<br /> <br /> Anyway, Blackfire PCs work like other VALKYRIE agents, complete with Advanced Armory, but take contracts, not only acting against the supernatural for other governments and wealthy interests, but also FOR wealthy supernaturals against others. As long as a given contract doesn't conflict with VALKYRIE's defense of the Republic (and its interests abroad), they have pretty free reign.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T20:12:03-07:00","id":127945,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>glamourweaver</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/127255-the-mercenaries?p=127944#post127944\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> At my own table, I've reimagined Blackfire as the private-sector arm of VALKYRIE - they're one of the Contractors that form the steering committee and actually oversee and fund VALKYRIE from within the Military Industrial Complex (Vampires are not in-charge of VALKYRIE, but several of these contractors are complicit with vampiric financial interests, and do &quot;keep the peace&quot; by steering VALKYRIE in directions away from those interests and toward their enemies).<br /> <br /> Anyway, Blackfire PCs work like other VALKYRIE agents, complete with Advanced Armory, but take contracts, not only acting against the supernatural for other governments and wealthy interests, but also FOR wealthy supernaturals against others. As long as a given contract doesn't conflict with VALKYRIE's defense of the Republic (and its interests abroad), they have pretty free reign.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is a pretty clever idea. Was it bought out by VALKYRIE or has it always existed as part of their program?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\">-: <b><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations\" target=\"_blank\">First Tongue Translation Requests</a></b> :-</div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1874-sikla-alkis","name":"Sikla Alkis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1874_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"833"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-07T20:34:21-07:00","id":127949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sikla Alkis</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/127255-the-mercenaries?p=127945#post127945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is a pretty clever idea. Was it bought out by VALKYRIE or has it always existed as part of their program?</div> </div> </div> </div>They're predecessor corp was one of the military contractors that successfully usurped control of VALKYRIE at the end of the Eisenhower Administration (the last President to know about VALKYRIE).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my expansion to the <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/185084-autochthonia-house-material\" target=\"_blank\">Realm of Brass and Shadow</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1098-glamourweaver","name":"glamourweaver","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1098_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"7541"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-17T13:45:59-07:00","id":140904,"title":"","content":"I think a really compelling idea for a Compact would be a PMC that fills a roll similar to that of the Wild Geese from Hellsing: a bunch of mercenaries hired by monsters to kill other monsters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3042-weaponwife","name":"WeaponWife","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-20T20:41:42-07:00","id":144055,"title":"","content":"Idunno if it'd fit as a compact, mercenaries seem...less organized. And a lot of hunters aren't the type that can pay outsiders to solve their problems (or if they could, wouldn't, like Ashwood Abbey or Cheiron).<br /> <br /> That said I like the idea of mercenaries for hunters. But why not work for other splats, for instance vampires or mages, who may be wealthy and more willing to have people solve their problems for them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 05-20-2014, 11:44 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}